  "equipment_type": "Boiler burner management interface",
  "applies_to": "Boilers with an SCC/Siemens TS-1100 touchscreen fronting LMV3 or LMV5 burner management and RWF40/55 controllers, read over Modbus RTU by a BASgatewayLX.",
  "summary": "Gateway profile for the TS-1100 touchscreen: 130 objects (66 AI, 6 AO, 58 BI), all polled. Binary inputs show the BMS connection, boiler available, pump status and the LMV and RWF input/output states plus annunciator inputs; six outputs set LMV and RWF remote mode, remote setpoint and remote output; analog inputs give LMV phase, actuator positions, output, setpoint/actual value, flame signal and lockout history.",
  "bacnet_transport": [
    "BACnet IP"
  ],
  "firmware": null,
  "default_device_instance": null,
  "access_inferred": true,
  "notes": [
    "Built from Contemporary Controls' BASgatewayLX Modbus device profile TS1100TouchS_RTU_LMV3_LMV5_RWF_a_LX.csv; the profile maps the registers in the TS-1100 Modbus RTU point list (https://www.ccontrols.com/support/dp/TS-1100_Installation_Instructions.pdf).",
    "Object instances are the ones this profile assigns when it is loaded into the gateway. A site that edited or rebuilt the profile may use different instances.",
    "All 130 rows are flagged for polling in the profile, so every object is served to BACnet once the profile is loaded.",
    "The CSV has no read/write column: Analog/Binary Inputs are read-only and Analog/Binary Outputs are commandable (priority array), which is how the gateway maps them (access inferred). Descriptions give the Modbus register each object reads."
  ],
  "source": {
